{"id":10110,"name":"graveler-alola","speciesId":75,"dex":75,"form":"alolan","generation":1,"types":["rock","electric"],"stats":{"hp":55,"attack":95,"defense":115,"special-attack":45,"special-defense":45,"speed":35},"abilities":[{"name":"magnet-pull","hidden":false},{"name":"sturdy","hidden":false},{"name":"galvanize","hidden":true}],"height":10,"weight":1100,"baseExp":137,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10110.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/10110.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/10110.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/10110.ogg","genus":"Rock Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon Rocha","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"Rolls down slopes to move. It rolls over any obstacle without slowing or changing its direction."},{"version":"yellow","text":"Often seen rolling down mountain trails. Obstacles are just things to roll straight over, not avoid."},{"version":"gold","text":"With a free and uncaring nature, it doesn't mind if pieces break off while it rolls down mountains."},{"version":"silver","text":"A slow walker, it rolls to move. It pays no attention to any object that happens to be in its path."},{"version":"crystal","text":"It travels by rol­ ling on mountain paths. If it gains too much speed, it stops by running into huge rocks."},{"version":"ruby","text":"GRAVELER grows by feeding on rocks. Apparently, it prefers to eat rocks that are covered in moss. This POKéMON eats its way through a ton of rocks on a daily basis."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"Rocks are GRAVELER’s favorite food. This POKéMON will climb a mountain from the base to the summit, crunchingly feasting on rocks all the while. Upon reaching the peak, it rolls back down to the bottom."},{"version":"emerald","text":"They descend from mountains by tumbling down steep slopes. They are so brutal, they smash aside obstructing trees and massive boulders with thunderous tackles."},{"version":"firered","text":"Be careful while hiking on mountain trails. GRAVELER may come rolling down the path without slowing."},{"version":"diamond","text":"GRAVELER make their homes on sheer cliff faces by gouging out numerous horizontal holes."},{"version":"pearl","text":"It tumbles down slopes, heedless of any body parts chipping off. It eats a ton of rocks daily."},{"version":"platinum","text":"It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no Pokémon can stop it without difficulty."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"With a free and uncaring nature, it doesn’t mind if pieces break off while it rolls down mountains."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Graveler grows by feeding on rocks. Apparently, it prefers to eat rocks that are covered in moss. This Pokémon eats its way through a ton of rocks on a daily basis."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Rocks are Graveler’s favorite food. This Pokémon will climb a mountain from the base to the summit, crunchingly feasting on rocks all the while. Upon reaching the peak, it rolls back down to the bottom."},{"version":"sun","text":"Mossy rocks are its favorite food. It can devour a ton a day while crunching loudly."},{"version":"moon","text":"This slow-footed Pokémon moves by curling up and rolling instead of walking. With enough momentum, its speed can exceed 60 mph."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"It climbs up cliffs as it heads toward the peak of a mountain. As soon as it reaches the summit, it rolls back down the way it came."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"It travels by rolling down cliffs. If it falls into a river, it will explode with its last gasp."},{"version":"legends-arceus","text":"Dwells in holes dug into sheer walls of stone. It enjoys rolling down slopes as though it were a boulder during a rockfall, so keep an eye upward while traversing mountain roads."}],"flavorPt":"Habita em buracos escavados em paredes íngremes de pedra. Ele gosta de rolar pelas encostas como se fosse uma pedra durante a queda de uma rocha, então fique de olho para cima enquanto atravessa estradas de montanha.","genderRate":4,"captureRate":120,"eggGroups":["mineral"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"geodude","speciesId":74,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Nível 25","Nível 25"],"species":"graveler","speciesId":75,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Troca","Troca"],"species":"golem","speciesId":76,"evolvesTo":[]}]}]},"varieties":[{"id":75,"name":"graveler","form":"normal","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/75.png"},{"id":10110,"name":"graveler-alola","form":"alolan","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10110.png"}],"games":[17,18,19,25],"moves":[{"id":7,"learn":[[18,"tutor",0],[19,"tm",0],[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":9,"learn":[[17,"lv",22],[18,"lv",22],[18,"tutor",0],[19,"lv",31],[19,"tm",0],[25,"lv",22],[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":29,"learn":[[19,"tm",0]]},{"id":33,"learn":[[17,"lv",1],[18,"lv",1],[19,"lv",1],[25,"lv",1]]},{"id":34,"learn":[[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":36,"learn":[[19,"lv",15],[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":38,"learn":[[17,"lv",50],[18,"lv",50],[19,"lv",39],[25,"lv",50],[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":53,"learn":[[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0],[19,"tm",0],[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":68,"learn":[[25,"egg",0]]},{"id":69,"learn":[[19,"tm",0]]},{"id":84,"learn":[[19,"lv",1],[19,"lv",3]]},{"id":85,"learn":[[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0],[19,"tm",0],[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":86,"learn":[[19,"tm",0],[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":87,"learn":[[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0],[19,"tm",0],[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":88,"learn":[[17,"lv",16],[18,"lv",16],[19,"lv",9],[25,"lv",16]]},{"id":89,"learn":[[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0],[19,"tm",0],[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":91,"learn":[[19,"tm",0],[25,"tm",0]]},{"id":92,"learn":[[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0],[19,"tm",0]]},{"id":103,"learn":[[25,"egg",0]]},{